rivals.needs_from_pair_matrix:
For at least one Zen runner (3, 4 or 5) and at least one Intel runner (an 8370C, and an 8573C if it can be had), sibling CPUs {0,1}, with cross-core {0,2} as the both-cores-busy baseline:

1. The walk (room, incl. assembly) beside, each as a factor over alone:
   - idle;
   - a second room walk on its own T-vector (f_W|W, the decisive row);
   - MTF;
   - build;
   - scanner (or the L1 ALU loop as its proxy);
   - RLE1+CRC (or the streaming read as its proxy).
   From these, f_W|N = Σ w_k f_W|k, with w_k from the phases four-copy rows of the same model.

2. The reverse rows, which the compute-side term needs and which swing ±4 points:
   - MTF beside the walk, and beside MTF;
   - build beside the walk, and beside build;
   - scanner beside the walk, and beside scanner.

3. Both members' rates in every pair, so that pair throughput (walk+X) can be read directly, not only the measured stage's slowdown.

4. A consistency check per model: s_W f_W|W + (1 - s_W) f_W|N must reproduce the OBSERVED mixed F_W (2.12 on the 7763, 2.22 on the 9V74, 1.46 on the 8370C) within about 0.1. If it fails, the probes do not represent the production mix, and the construction-level gate (prototype step A) decides instead.

5. Decision rule:
   - Compute G = -[s_W(1 - f_W|N/F_W) + s_N(1 - f_N|W/F_N)] per model. Use sim.py with the measured matrix in place of the patterns when the two sides are imbalanced.
   - |G| < 3% on every model measured: outcome C. Reject; journal entry and a line in the Rejected list.
   - G ≤ -5% on any CI model, and no model worse than +2%: run step A, then B.
   - Note that f_W|W ≤ 2.2 on AMD, with mixed 2.12-2.22, already caps the AMD walk term at about 2%. The walk|walk row alone can therefore reject most of the AMD case.

collision.matrix_requirements:
THE CELLS THAT DECIDE (each reported as a factor over alone, ±0.10-0.15)
Measured member on CPU 0. Sibling on CPU 1, plus a cross-core control on CPU 2. The other core is run both idle and loaded with a production mix (two free-running chain loops), so the L3 load matches 4t.
- Measured members:
  - W = walk_segments_room on real blocks, with a T-vector freshly built per block so that L2 residency matches production;
  - W' = room_segments without assembly;
  - MTF;
  - build;
  - scanner (Scanner::next over the corpus);
  - RLE1+CRC;
  - assembly on its own.
- Siblings:
  - idle;
  - PAUSE spin [MISSING: an active thread using almost no resources];
  - L1 ALU loop;
  - L1 store stream at 2 stores a cycle into 8 KiB [MISSING];
  - plain chain;
  - 32-lane L2-resident chase [MISSING, walk.md NEXT probe (i)];
  - streaming read;
  - MTF;
  - build;
  - scanner;
  - RLE1+CRC;
  - W on a different block, free-running;
  - W on the same block, started together [MISSING: the phases alignment];
  - duty-cycled ALU, 50% busy / 50% futex-parked, period 0.2-2 ms [MISSING: short idles].
- Both members' rates over the same interval, so pair throughput can be read directly, with every sibling looping its own stage in steady state.
- Kernel axis [MISSING]: the gather walk and the one-store variant as measured members beside idle, PAUSE and themselves, plus their rows in the 4-copy walk-only sweep.

MISSING OUTSIDE THE MATRIX (cheap, and independent of the outcome)
1. Each runner's guest idle path: /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpuidle current_driver, current_governor_ro, the state names and latencies, and /proc/cmdline. Free to add to env.json. This settles shared assumption 3 together with the duty-cycle cell.
2. The production decoder's sibling-resolved walk-beside-walk share:
- add a WalkStart mark between build and walk;
- record sched_getcpu() at the stage marks in the occupancy tool;
- also record per-block walk start and end in a 2-copy {0,1} phases run.
This is trace-only and full tier. It tells whether today's decoder is walk-locked (the M/P dynamics) or randomly paired.
3. C3's absorption probe: one thread, sibling halted, the room walk with an MTF cursor and a scanner cursor interleaved every 8, 16 or 32 lanes, budget in moves. It reports e = (T_walk + T_mtf + T_scan - T_interleaved) / (T_mtf + T_scan). The matrix cannot measure e.

COVERAGE
- The 7763 (Zen 3) and the 9V74 (Zen 4) separately: the priors differ (7763 C-like: slope 0.14, decoder/phases x1.017; 9V74 weak P: slope 0.50, decoder/phases 0.92).
- The 8370C.
- The 8573C if it lands (the master bench's runner, which has no factors at all).
- The 9V45 (Zen 5, with the largest partitions) as the model that discriminates the partition reading.
- One repeat on the same model, against serial-stages' stability threshold of 0.2.
- Report the median of rounds as well as the fastest, since fastest-of-N favours lucky alignment.

DECISION CONDITIONS (registered before the run)
- C: every light sibling Y in {PAUSE, ALU, MTF, scanner} has |f(W|Y) - f(W|W)| <= 0.2 on both Zen models.
  - Partition mechanism if also f(W|PAUSE) >= f(W|W) - 0.2.
  - Store-queue contention if f(W|store stream) - f(W|ALU) >= 0.3.
  - Miss-buffer contention if f(W|L2 chase) - f(W|ALU) >= 0.3.
- M: f(W|Y) <= 1.3 for Y in {PAUSE, ALU, MTF, scanner}, and >= 1.8 for Y in {build, stream, walk}.
- P: not M, and δ_eff = f(W|W) - Σ w_k f(W|k) >= 0.3. Weights for the compute thread's mix: scanner 0.21, MTF 0.32, build 0.37, RLE1+CRC 0.10 on the 7763; 0.20 / 0.31 / 0.40 / 0.09 on the 9V74.
- C1 vs C2 under M or P:
  - compute-side contrasts: cw = f(N|W) - f(N|N) for MTF, build and scanner;
  - C2's own rule: δ_eff - 1.3·cw >= 0.4;
  - the memory token if f(B|W) - f(B|M) >= 0.4.
- Lock: a walk-beside-walk share >= 0.75 (decoder or 2-copy) means lock, and G must be computed against the locked today. A share <= 0.6 means no lock.
- Short idle: if f(W|duty) > 0.5 (1 + f(W|ALU)) + 0.1, short idles poll, and every design's idle credit is void.
- Consistency:
  - (a) Σ_Y p_Y f(W|Y) with the phases shares and the measured lock reproduces F_W (2.12 / 2.22 / 1.46) within 0.1;
  - (b) with the occupancy shares it reproduces the decoder's 4t/1t CPU per block within 3%.
  If (a) passes and (b) fails, predict from the decoder's mix.
- Predictions are re-run with the measured table in place of the patterns (sim.py for C1, des.py for C2), against the decoder's today.

collision.plan_by_outcome:
ALL PREDICTED FIGURES BELOW ARE INFERRED (modelled), as 4t wall against master, with the 0.93 dilution and each design's overhead included. Nothing below is measured.

FIRST, OUTCOME-INDEPENDENT AND CHEAP (full tier, by hand)
- The guest idle-path record.
- The sibling-resolved walk-beside-walk share (occupancy WalkStart mark + sched_getcpu).
- The gather walk and the one-store walk as rows in the 4-copy walk-only sweep on a Zen 3/4 runner and an Intel runner.

(C) ANY BUSY SIBLING COSTS THE WALK ABOUT 2x
- Modelled bounds:
  - C1: -4.5% to +7.8%, central +1.5% (its own, plus 0 to +3% for floaters);
  - C2: AMD -2.5% to +5.8% (central +1%), Intel -0.4% to +8.5% (+3%);
  - C3 corrected: 7763 +4% to +15% (slower), 9V74 -6% to +6%, central about 0;
  - window-light walk: AMD 0 to -20% (central -3% to -8%), Intel -3% to +2%.
- Prototype first: the window-light walk (the third possibility), switched on by the plan only where threads > physical cores.
- Gate 0, the 4-copy sweep: variant/room <= 0.95 at 4 copies, 95% CI excluding 1.0, on a Zen 3 or Zen 4 runner; no model above 1.03. If it fails: a journal entry and a Rejected line.
- PR-bench rule (registered):
  - 4t wall faster, 95% interval excluding 0, on an AMD runner;
  - 4t CPU falls by at least as much as wall (the #171 co-run signature);
  - 1t and 2t within noise (the same code path, as A/A controls);
  - parity passes;
  - RSS within noise.
- Falsifier: not faster beyond noise in two AMD runs when gate 0 predicted >= 5%.
- If the window-light walk fails: run C3's absorption probe. Build C3 only if e >= 0.7 on a Zen 4 and >= 0.6 on the 7763, with the rule "2t wall cut by >= 1 - 1/S_runner (S = master's 4t/2t speedup, 1.13-1.24, so a 12-19% cut), and 4t faster with 95% CI excluding 0, AMD only".
- Reject C1 and C2: journal entry plus Rejected line.

(M) ONLY MEMORY-HEAVY SIBLINGS COST
- Modelled bounds:
  - C1 corrected (re-paired today, floaters): AMD -10% to -19% (central -14%), Intel -3% to -12% (central -6%);
  - C2 walk token: AMD -11% to +2% (central -3.5%; -9.5% at C1's strong M); memory token -7% to -13%;
  - C3: dominated.
- Prototype first: C1, with three fixes:
  - pin to the core's 2-CPU mask, with roles enforced by the queues;
  - floaters biased to the compute CPUs;
  - step A run with the thread layout that would ship.
- Gate: G <= -5% from the measured table; step A staged/full >= 1.05 with CI excluding 1 on AMD, and no model below 0.98.
- PR-bench rule (registered):
  - 4t wall faster, 95% interval excluding 0;
  - prediction registered at AMD -10% to -17%, Intel -3% to -8%;
  - 1t and 2t as null controls (C1 does not engage there);
  - 4t CPU falls about as wall does;
  - parity passes;
  - RSS up to +5% (about +2 MB, weighed for a 16 GB laptop).
- Comparator arms (full tier): C2's memory token, only if f(B|W) - f(B|M) >= 0.4.
- The window-light walk can run in parallel: it is orthogonal.

(P) WALK BESIDE COMPUTE IS MATERIALLY CHEAPER THAN WALK BESIDE WALK
- Modelled bounds:
  - C2: AMD -15% to 0% (central -5%), Intel -6.5% to +1%;
  - C1 corrected: AMD -1% to -12% (central -5%), Intel +2% to -9% (central -2%);
  - C3: dominated.
- Prototype first: C2's walk token.
  - Its patch exists. Compile and test it under flock first (check.sh, Miri on pairs::tests).
  - It pins to the core mask.
  - It is symmetric, so it degrades to today's behaviour when the token is free.
  - The memory token is a one-line extension.
- Gate: δ_eff - 1.3·cw >= 0.4 on an AMD model; des.py re-run with the measured table predicts <= -3.5%.
- PR-bench rule (registered):
  - 4t wall faster, 95% interval excluding 0. Two runs if the prediction is between -3% and -5%: 4t resolves only to ±2-5%;
  - 1t and 2t unchanged (place() returns None on CPUs 0,2);
  - 4t CPU falls about as wall does;
  - parity passes;
  - RSS up by 2-4 MB, accepted;
  - a full-tier "pin only" arm separates pinning from the token.
- Engage on Intel only if its own measured δ predicts <= -3%.
- Keep C1 in reserve, for the case where the measured compute-side rows favour it (f(N|W) < f(N|N) - 0.1).
